WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.649
"Risks and Benefits of
Nicotinamide Mononucleotide (NMN), a NAD+ Booster"

00:00:07.115 --> 00:00:11.920
Both NR and NMN have been shown
to have beneficial effects in rodents,

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.400
though they haven’t
been tested side-by-side.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.280
Both precursors raise blood
levels of NAD+ in people

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.120
but similarly haven’t been pitted
head-to-head against one another.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.080
One potential advantage
of NMN over NR

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.360
is that it may be more
stable in the bloodstream.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:31.520
In mouse blood at least, within an hour,
most NR is converted into NAM,

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.720
whereas NMN levels remain steady.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:39.240
You could also argue that NMN is better
because it’s a direct precursor of NAD+,

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.800
whereas NR first has
to be converted to NMN;

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.800
so, we might as well just
take NMN in the first place.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:49.600
Ironically, the exact opposite
argument can also be made

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.360
based on the inability of NMN to
pass through cell membranes.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:59.120
Structurally, NMN is just NR with
a phosphate group attached to it.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:02.920
The phosphate charge prevents NMN
from passing in and out of cells;

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.960
so, to get inside a cell, NMN first
has to be converted into NR.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:12.400
Then, once inside, the NR can turn
back into NMN and make NAD+.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:18.080
So, if NMN first has to be converted
into NR for cell entry, the argument goes,

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:21.120
maybe you might as well
just take NR to begin with,

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.960
because there’s no
NMN transporter.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.360
Or is there?

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:29.440
An NMN transporter was recently
described (at least in mouse intestine);

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.560
so, maybe NMN is
able to skip the NR step

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:36.000
and pass directly into cells
to make NAD+ after all.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.000
However, the evidence that such a NMN
transporter exists remains controversial.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.000
NMN boasts a long list of
rodent healthspan benefits,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.080
but, unlike NR, has yet to demonstrate
an extension of mammalian lifespan.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.800
What about in people?

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.160
There have just been a few human
NMN studies published to date.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:59.040
One small study of healthy
middle-aged men

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.600
found that various single doses
had no apparent effect

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:05.520
on any of the measured variables,
including retinal eye function,

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.520
sleep quality, heart rate,
blood pressure,

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.640
oxygenation,
or body temperature.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:13.640
A 12-week study of daily NMN supplementation
in middle-aged men and women

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:17.520
similarly found no significant
effects on any outcome,

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.680
including lean mass,
muscle mass, body fat,

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:22.480
blood sugars, cholesterol,
or insulin sensitivity.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:27.040
NMN did boost blood NAD+ levels,
though they peaked after the first month

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.400
and then trended down
for months two and three;

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.080
so, there may have been an
adaptive drop in NAD+ synthesis

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:35.240
as was suspected with NR.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:40.920
Like NR, NMN also fails to
raise NAD+ in muscle tissue.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.960
One study evocatively entitled,

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:48.400
“Nicotinamide Mononucleotide Supplementation
Enhances Aerobic Capacity in Amateur Runners,”

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.880
tested three different doses of
NMN versus placebo for six weeks

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.840
among young and middle-
aged recreational runners.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:01.240
Aerobic capacity was increased at one
ventilatory threshold, but not the other.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:04.240
No overall benefit for aerobic
capacity or peak power

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:08.240
or any of another ten measures of
cardiopulmonary function was found.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:09.680
If you measure enough things,

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:12.480
statistical outliers,
both positive and negative ones,

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.160
can just pop up as flukes.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.800
For example, the researchers
noted significant improvement

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.520
in the single-leg stance test,

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:23.900
but the NMN had no significant effect on
any of the other physical function tests.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.640
And upon closer inspection,

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:30.080
the apparent single-leg balance benefit
was only found in the middle-dose group

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.360
compared to the high-dose group,

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:36.920
because the high-dose group ended up
doing slightly worse compared to baseline.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:41.440
No significant effect was found for
any of the doses compared to placebo.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:46.680
A similar issue can be found in a 12-week
study of NMN supplementation in older adults.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.880
The NMN company-funded
authors concluded

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:55.240
that NMN “improved lower limb function
and reduced drowsiness in older adults.”

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:58.680
But it failed to significantly
affect 16 additional measures,

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:02.760
including other tests of lower
limb function and fatigue.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:08.480
There are so few NMN studies that this
kind of shotgun approach is understandable,

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:12.040
casting the widest possible net
for effects to be further tested,

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:17.280
but on their own cannot be presented
as convincing proof of efficacy.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:21.040
All of the above NMN studies
were on healthy individuals.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:25.600
What about testing NMN on those who
are already metabolically compromised?

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:28.440
Overweight or obese postmenopausal
women with prediabetes

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:32.200
were randomized to NMN
or placebo for 10 weeks.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:35.720
NMN didn’t seem to affect
body weight or composition,

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:38.760
liver fat, blood pressure,
or a dozen other metabolic variables,

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:41.960
but it did improve
muscle insulin sensitivity,

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:47.720
though not enough to affect insulin levels
or short- or long-term blood sugar control.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:53.440
This may be because insulin sensitivity
in the liver and body fat remained unchanged.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:56.840
NMN also appeared to have no
effect on mitochondrial function

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:59.640
or muscle strength,
fatigability, or recovery.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:06.160
In terms of safety, NMN shills speak of it as
being naturally found in fruits and vegetables,

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:10.200
but even the most concentrated sources
(edamame, avocado, and broccoli)

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:16.560
have over a hundred times less per serving
than the typical NMN supplement dose.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:21.360
The same could be said for NR in milk
(human and otherwise).

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:26.680
There are safety evaluations for NMN
on rats and dogs, but unlike NR,

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:33.480
supplemental doses of NMN have yet to
be shown as safe for human consumption.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.920
There are rodent studies
showing that NMN

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:39.320
may have negative metabolic
consequences compared to placebo,

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:44.200
but the most serious concern
is nerve degeneration.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:48.160
The accumulation of NMN
in nerve cells is toxic.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.880
Since NR is converted into NMN,

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:54.880
this is a major concern for
NR supplementation as well.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:57.960
The type of nerve damage,
axon degeneration,

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:02.440
is a major contributor to a variety
of neurodegenerative disorders.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:08.440
Blocking an NMN-synthesizing enzyme
appeared to help damaged neurons in vitro,

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:11.880
protection that’s abolished
by adding NMN back,

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:16.400
and adding an enzyme that chews up
NMN was also found to be protective,

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:22.040
further supporting a theory of degenerative
effects of accumulating NMN.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:25.120
However, clinical effects
remain theoretical,

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:29.560
as these adverse effects have only been
demonstrated in fish, mice, and petri dishes.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:35.160
Of course, NMN supplements may not
even have NMN in the first place.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:39.920
ChromaDex, which sells the rival
supplement Tru Niagen (a form of NR),

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:45.080
claims to have tested the 22 NMN brands
with the highest market share on Amazon

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:48.920
and found that most had
virtually no NMN at all.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:53.080
Ironically, many of the apparently fake
NMN products displayed quote-unquote

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:58.120
“certificates of analysis” and carried
hundreds or thousands of positive reviews.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:05.400
Evidently, only 3 out of 22 were found to contain
as much NMN as advertised on their label.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:08.440
Of course, ChromaDex isn’t
above being shady itself;

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:11.640
it’s been accused of making
hyped false claims for Tru Niagen

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:15.360
by both the FDA and the
Better Business Bureau.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:20.520
In short, NR has been demonstrated
to be relatively safe but not effective,

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:25.935
and neither safety nor efficacy
has been established for NMN.

